  "constraints": [
    "Frozen joint168 across 16 ranks. IDs are bound to the previous seed, next target and same-stream op motifs established by a separate frame-bearing capture. Missing motif earns no credit. Named kernel durations and dispatch API intervals are alternatives; each wave can use its most favorable scheduled rank and assumes savings fully translate in series. Incoming state before current target, outgoing draft setup follows current sampling. Inclusive first-chunk cutoff may overcredit that last outgoing wave.",
    "State replaces two regions: (1) use prior seed/draft and request-specific suffixes to patch current IDs, (2) derive computed, accepted, ordinary positions, seq lengths and independent tail. Retain raw draft read before sanitize, original count D2H, qsl/H2D, slot mappings, CP lengths and graph banks. Sanitize three-task erasure is a separate upper scenario. State device/API arms delete all matched old tasks with zero replacement. Actual two-dispatch plan retains work, validated old-row bounds, input generation and safe cross-row read-before-write. Do not merge across unknown readiness.",
    "Main-thread CPU proxy: 48 archived B4/D20/24 full-signature rank calls. Deduplicate the CPU records attached to each old task and union their wall intervals on the worker main thread. Subtract two median matched CPU wrapper intervals per call for two replacement dispatches. Transfer rank median net to matching same-request-set steady B4 waves, using pooled median on unsampled ranks. Within-wave maximum, full serial exposure. CPU/API/device all overlap, never sum. Wall intervals include profiler effects and waits; required main-thread or critical-path improvement on the newer configuration has not been measured.",
    "Draft setup erasure includes matched context TensorMove, typed arithmetic/fills adjacent to first-pass copy and known unused position gather. Existing multi-output copy/expand and all three WKV panels remain. Other seed, slot and padding outputs, untyped DMA, block-table clone and callback/host orchestration receive no credit. Fills need their distinct bounds; positive time is a screening allowance only.",
    "Window sensitivity applies only to long per-request segments. Keep min(U,128) per request including full short verification spans. Requires the same request/cache generation, row demand of all three layers and retirement of prefix, future/resume and peer readers. If windows or other observers differ, retain their union. Raw and after-writer scenarios hold all TP communication, weight placement, initial checkpoint gathers, shape-dependent numerical equivalence and other work fixed. Costs include main GEMM/transpose/RMS and three WKV device-task sums. Exclude gaps, subtract replacement median interpolated in row count; after-writer uses the prior direct_writer_100pct median credit at the same q. Row elimination is conditional pruning separate from fusion. Identifying retained rows, packing them and changed matmul tiling may remove the gain. No claim the truncated rows are safe from the profile alone.",
    "Ordinary single-request projections interpolate one prompt through two measured surrounding shapes. Each verification retains all six rows. State estimates transfer the largest matched B1 task cost across available samples to each archived verification. No B1 CPU timing transferred. Actual enabled workload mix, end-to-end speedup and host overhead remain unmeasured."
  ],
